    "# Quiz: Time series forecasting with ARIMA\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-2-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>ARIMA stands for</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>AutoRegressive Integral Moving Average</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The I stands for Integrated, not Integral.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>AutoRegressive Integrated Moving Action</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The MA stands for Moving Average, not Moving Action.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>AutoRegressive Integrated Moving Average</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. ARIMA stands for AutoRegressive Integrated Moving Average.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-2-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Stationarity refers to</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>data whose attributes does not change when shifted in time</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Stationarity is about the data's distribution, which does not change when shifted in time.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>data whose distribution does not change when shifted in time</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Stationary data has a distribution that does not change when shifted in time.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>data whose distribution changes when shifted in time</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. It is the reverse. Stationary data's distribution does not change when shifted in time.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-2-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Differencing</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>stabilizes trend and seasonality</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Differencing removes trend and seasonality. What it stabilizes is the mean of the time series.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>exacerbates trend and seasonality</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Differencing does not make trend and seasonality worse. It removes them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>eliminates trend and seasonality</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Differencing removes changes in the level of a time series, which eliminates trend and seasonality.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-2-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>ARIMA is used to make a model fit the special form of time series data</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>as flat as possible</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The goal is a close fit to the data, not a flat one.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>as closely as possible</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. ARIMA's goal is a model that fits the time series data as closely as possible.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>via scatterplots</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. ARIMA is about fitting a model to the time series data as closely as possible, not about making scatterplots.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-2-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Use SARIMAX to</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>manage seasonal ARIMA models</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Data with a seasonal pattern needs a seasonal ARIMA model, which you build by calling SARIMAX().</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>manage special ARIMA models</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. SARIMAX is for data with a seasonal pattern. It builds a seasonal ARIMA model.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>manage statistical ARIMA models</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. SARIMAX is for data with a seasonal pattern. It builds a seasonal ARIMA model.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-7-2-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>'Walk-Forward' validation involves</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>re-evaluating a model progressively as it is validated</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Each prediction is checked, but the key idea is that the model is re-trained each time new data arrives.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>re-training a model progressively as it is validated</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. In walk-forward validation, the model is re-trained each time new data becomes available.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>re-configuring a model progressively as it is validated</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Walk-forward validation re-trains the model each time new data becomes available.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
